    {
      "commit": "c5be5bf0ca6c9bd717ac805f9a2071bc282b697a",
      "disposition": "adapted",
      "rationale": "Retain the lockdep API relocation, old sync-level re-exports, explicit static constructor and Send implementation as prerequisites for static raw-spinlock/rate-limit initialization. This is not only a file move: the constructor makes static pin/no-Drop obligations explicit and Send permits moving pinned ownership between tasks without moving its allocation. Native lockdep register/unregister synchronization remains unchanged, and public as_ptr still places raw-pointer validity obligations on the caller. Omit the purely maintainer-ownership entry, consistently with the port metadata policy. SDK disables DEBUG_LOCK_ALLOC; that configuration does not justify removing source compatibility for Android diagnostic configurations. Non-SDK configurations and documentation examples were not compiled.",
      "result_commits": [
        "2fbc2da4ade330c86d97491696f9223c9df7bc8f"
      ],
      "evidence": [
