    {
      "commit": "8d1f524115e325feff1fc7740a719c9b1b5f6542",
      "disposition": "adapted",
      "rationale": "Retain the raw-spinlock const initializer and raw lockdep map construction required by static Rust rate limiters. The selected x86 SMP arch_spinlock_t is a qspinlock whose unlocked native initializer is all zero; the Rust constructor uses that value. Debug magic, owner CPU/pointer sentinels and wait-type fields match native C initializers by source inspection, with LD_WAIT_INV equal to zero. Current SDK disables DEBUG_SPINLOCK and DEBUG_LOCK_ALLOC; other listed architectures and alternative debug configurations are not claimed compiled. Shared cfg branches are retained within the required generic constructor, without adding another platform driver. Native lock operations and lock layout are unchanged.",
      "result_commits": [
        "2fbc2da4ade330c86d97491696f9223c9df7bc8f"
      ],
      "evidence": [
