    {
      "commit": "6efd82a128d8df28bdefb7b6991c8a914919fd57",
      "disposition": "adapted",
      "rationale": "Retain pinned Ratelimit, static per-callsite state, initialization/exit helpers and all pr_*_ratelimited macros for selected Rust Binder diagnostics. State initialization matches native RATELIMIT_STATE_INIT, including zero flags/counters and native defaults of 5*HZ and burst 10. ___ratelimit owns synchronization and remains exactly LTS, including its current atomic budget, contention and interval-reset behavior. The macro evaluates print arguments only if admitted; selected uses are diagnostics, not functional side effects. pr_debug preserves debug-assertion gating. Suppression can hide repeated diagnostic lines, intentionally limiting caller-induced log flooding; no lossless diagnostic stream is promised. Pinned dynamic state and static-only constructor preserve internal lock addresses.",
